# TLS_MODE=external-host: your reverse proxy runs on another host and holds the certificate.
# It forwards to this host's published HTTP_PORT (docker-compose.external-host.yml).
# Plain HTTP only: no certificates, no ACME, no local CA, nothing on 443.
# Any Host name is answered. Set UPSTREAM_PROXIES to the proxy host's IP/CIDR;
# only that address range is believed about who the client is.
http:// {
        import site
}
